 "sceneStyle": "Unified visual style for all scenes: cinematic photographic realism, a contemporary Chinese metropolis, inside and around a modern glass-curtain-wall office tower at night or pre-dawn. Cold teal-green fluorescent palette, glass reflections and chrome, ONE warm accent light per frame (vending machine glow / lobby uplight / phone screen / green exit sign). Sterile corporate interiors with a subtle surreal unease like the TV series \"Severance\": empty corridors, potted sansevieria and areca palms, mop buckets, buzzing ventilation, faint red standby LEDs in the dark. Slight film grain, muted colors, wide 16:9 cinematic composition, dry deadpan suspense tone. ABSOLUTELY NO text, letters, numbers, captions or watermarks in the image.",
 "sceneCharacters": "Character and location sheet (keep consistent across scenes when present):\n- CHEN MO (陈默, protagonist): Chinese male early 30s, ex-tech-product-manager turned property manager, lean, short black hair, light blue property-management uniform shirt with lanyard work badge, calm observant expression, often holding a paper coffee cup or phone flashlight.\n- ZHOU YUN (周芸): admin-office woman mid 30s, neat ponytail, white blouse, oat-milk cup, unfazed tired expression.\n- XIAO MAN (小满): front-desk girl mid 20s, pink lipstick, reception counter, sweet but unreadable smile.\n- ZHAO PENGFEI (赵鹏飞): property manager mid 40s, navy suit jacket, walkie-talkie, corporate double-chin.\n- WANG DEFA (王德发): day-shift security guard late 50s, warm grin, old-style guard uniform, guard booth.\n- THE TOWER: glass curtain wall reflecting city lights; three-story atrium with a huge areca palm and black piano; 7th-floor mezzanine corridor with floor-to-ceiling windows; dim annex building with narrow tiled corridors, peeling paint dust; a hidden \"9.5th floor\" equipment level with red indicator LEDs and humming machines; dead potted pothos with dying leaves."
